Line 2: How often has to be a number, but this is text.
    every speed seconds:
          ^^^^^

Line 4: An event needs yes or no to decide, but this is text.
    whenever speed:
             ^^^^^
Compare it with something, like "whenever score is over 100".

Line 7: "every" can only be at the top level, not inside an "if" or a loop.
        every 2 seconds:
        ^^^^^
Move it to the start of a line, outside every block. Events run once the rest of the program has.

Line 10: "whenever" can only be at the top level, not inside a definition.
        whenever speed is "slow", say "w".
        ^^^^^^^^
Move it to the start of a line, outside every block. Events run once the rest of the program has.

Line 12: I can't add a number to text.
        say it plus 1.
            ^^^^^^^^^
To join text, use "followed by".
